  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "June Medical Services L.L.C.",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1323",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "15a627f5b660c8e6743efbf4e5044cacf5d7a20b82b785be496dd91e0e4178a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15a627f5b660-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. RIKELMAN: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: This case is about respect for the Court's precedent. Just four years ago, the Court held in Whole Woman's Health that the Texas admitting privileges law imposed an undue burden on women seeking abortions."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1323",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "15a627f5b660c8e6743efbf4e5044cacf5d7a20b82b785be496dd91e0e4178a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15a627f5b660-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Would you have done anything different if it had been -- if the third-party standing had been timely raised?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1323",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "15a627f5b660c8e6743efbf4e5044cacf5d7a20b82b785be496dd91e0e4178a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15a627f5b660-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: That sounds -- that sounds like a direct standing, not third-party standing. But in this case, is there anything like the conflict that Justice Alito had mentioned? Is there a conflict?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1323",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "15a627f5b660c8e6743efbf4e5044cacf5d7a20b82b785be496dd91e0e4178a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15a627f5b660-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 15,
        "start": 15
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: And might you have, if you had a timely notice, just as insurance, joined a patient or two?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1323",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "15a627f5b660c8e6743efbf4e5044cacf5d7a20b82b785be496dd91e0e4178a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15a627f5b660-0000-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 16,
        "start": 16
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: How many abortion cases has -- has the Court either expressly or silently allowed the doctors to sue on behalf of the women? I -- I counted eight, but maybe that's overstating it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1323",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "15a627f5b660c8e6743efbf4e5044cacf5d7a20b82b785be496dd91e0e4178a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15a627f5b660-0000-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: So he had -- he didn't have -- it would be counter to his own interests for him to make a super effort to get admitting privileges, wouldn't it, because he'd be defeating his own claim?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1323",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "15a627f5b660c8e6743efbf4e5044cacf5d7a20b82b785be496dd91e0e4178a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15a627f5b660-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: When Doe --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "State",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1323",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "15a627f5b660c8e6743efbf4e5044cacf5d7a20b82b785be496dd91e0e4178a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15a627f5b660-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Two, that the state's key credentialing expert conceded that physicians who never intended to treat patients in the hospital will not get privileges."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1323",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "15a627f5b660c8e6743efbf4e5044cacf5d7a20b82b785be496dd91e0e4178a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15a627f5b660-0001-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the district court found that this law would leave Louisiana with just one clinic in one state to serve about 10,000 people per year."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1323",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "15a627f5b660c8e6743efbf4e5044cacf5d7a20b82b785be496dd91e0e4178a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15a627f5b660-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Could an admitting privileges law of this kind ever have a valid purpose, in your view?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Murrill",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1323",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "15a627f5b660c8e6743efbf4e5044cacf5d7a20b82b785be496dd91e0e4178a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15a627f5b660-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. MURRILL: No, I don't think that it does at all. I mean, in our case it was demonstrably different. They could and did get privileges."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1323",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "15a627f5b660c8e6743efbf4e5044cacf5d7a20b82b785be496dd91e0e4178a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15a627f5b660-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Is it not the fact that most hospitals in Louisiana, in order to get admitting privileges, you have to admit a certain number of patients?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Murrill",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1323",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "15a627f5b660c8e6743efbf4e5044cacf5d7a20b82b785be496dd91e0e4178a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15a627f5b660-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. MURRILL: Yes. It is inaccurate because what the record demonstrated is that they don't know what their qualification -- what their complication rates are. They all testified that they don't know because women don't follow up with them or they don't follow up with women."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1323",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "15a627f5b660c8e6743efbf4e5044cacf5d7a20b82b785be496dd91e0e4178a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15a627f5b660-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: How does that differ from Craig against Boren?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1323",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "15a627f5b660c8e6743efbf4e5044cacf5d7a20b82b785be496dd91e0e4178a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15a627f5b660-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: I mean, that wasn't this case, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1323",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "15a627f5b660c8e6743efbf4e5044cacf5d7a20b82b785be496dd91e0e4178a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15a627f5b660-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Is it not -- is it not a reality, is it not really the fact, that almost all hospitals in the State of Louisiana do have an admission, you have to have an admission record in order to admit patients?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1323",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "15a627f5b660c8e6743efbf4e5044cacf5d7a20b82b785be496dd91e0e4178a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15a627f5b660-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Can that be done?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "June Medical Services",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1323",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "15a627f5b660c8e6743efbf4e5044cacf5d7a20b82b785be496dd91e0e4178a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15a627f5b660-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. RIKELMAN: Your Honor, the lack of benefits of these laws is not state-dependent. The medical consensus is clear that in no state do they serve health and safety benefits."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "District Court",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1323",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "15a627f5b660c8e6743efbf4e5044cacf5d7a20b82b785be496dd91e0e4178a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15a627f5b660-0003-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "court found that this law would be extremely burdensome, more so than the Texas law in Whole Woman's Health. And its finding that these physicians would not be able to get privileges is supported by at least four aspects of the record."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "District Court",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1323",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "15a627f5b660c8e6743efbf4e5044cacf5d7a20b82b785be496dd91e0e4178a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15a627f5b660-0003-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the fact that they tried to get privileges at 15 hospitals over one-and-a-half years under the court's supervision;"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1323",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "15a627f5b660c8e6743efbf4e5044cacf5d7a20b82b785be496dd91e0e4178a6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-15a627f5b660-0003-0006",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 71,
        "start": 71
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
